Modified: Topo modifies the fork, from 2026-09-22 to 2026-10-17, by the twelve patches in `patches/ish/`, each dated by the commit that added it: 0001 the memory brake's refresh hook (`kernel/mm.h`, `kernel/mmap.c`); 0002 the `offsets` source in `meson.build`; 0003 `pidfd_open` on an unreaped child (`kernel/pidfd.c`); 0004 the guest's own `mount` refused for the host's filesystem (`fs/mount.c`); 0005 the vector forms of SQABS and SQNEG, 0009 SMOV and 0010 the NEON decode gaps (`asbestos/guest-arm64`); 0006 the DNS stub's sentinel address (`fs/sock.c`, `fs/sock.h`); 0007 the block chaining's test of a free jump slot (`asbestos/asbestos.c`); 0008 a guest tmpfs unmounted rather than the app ended (`fs/tmp.c`); 0011 the mount lookup's cache read under its lock (`fs/mount.c`); 0012 a code store after a TLB miss (`asbestos/guest-arm64/gadgets-aarch64/entry.S`, `emu/tlb.c`, `emu/tlb.h`, `kernel/memory.c`, `kernel/memory.h`)
Use: The guest's kernel: an arm64 Linux userland run in the app's own process, its system calls answered by iSH's kernel and its code run by the Asbestos engine. Linked into the iOS app through `Packages/TopoUserland`; nothing boots it outside a debug launch and the tests. `Packages/TopoUserland/Guest/topo_ish.c` follows the fork's `app/AppDelegate.m` and `app/ISHShellExecutor.m` for the boot sequence, the anonymous-memory cap and the process launch, and is under the same terms. `Packages/TopoUserland/Guest/topo_vaultfs.m` follows the fork's `app/iOSFS.m` for the file coordination around realfs, and is under the same terms. The fork's `deps/linux` and `deps/libapps` are GPL code the waiver does not cover, and the build refuses a checkout that has either.

